id: pm-graph-l9df
title: Fix runGraph projected result narrowing and bump pm-cli to 2026.8.3
description: "pm-cli 2026.8.3 changed the SDK runGraph return type from GraphResult to ProjectedGraphResult (GraphResult plus an output projection declaration). The generic wrapper runPmGraph in src/index.ts casts that to an unresolved type parameter T, which fails typecheck with TS2352. Fix: remove the type parameter, return the projected result, and narrow on the subcommand discriminant at the single impact call site with a CommandError guard. Also bump the pm-cli pin to 2026.8.3 in devDependencies and peerDependencies with a committed lockfile refresh. Supersedes dependabot PR 51."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-03T22:03:05.195Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T23:16:13.687Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-03T23:15:58.920Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-03T23:15:58.920Z"
claim_principal: claude-code
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "npm run typecheck, build, test, coverage, and changelog:check all pass; no cast or any introduced; pin at 2026.8.3 in package.json and package-lock.json"
resolution: Return type derived from runGraph via Awaited<ReturnType<typeof runGraph>> instead of re-declaring the removed GraphResult union; generic parameter and its as-T assertion both removed.
expected_result: "pm-graph compiles and passes its full suite against the 2026.8.3 SDK, with no type assertion on the graph dispatch path and no locally re-declared copy of a host type."
actual_result: "Achieved. typecheck, build, tests and release:check (coverage, audit, pack, changelog) all pass against 2026.8.3. Merged as unbraind/pm-graph#53."
close_reason: "Merged in unbraind/pm-graph#53. The 2026.8.3 engine returns the ProjectedGraphResult union and no longer exports GraphResult/GraphImpactResult, so the return type is now derived from runGraph via Awaited<ReturnType<typeof runGraph>> rather than re-declared locally where a hand-maintained copy would drift. That also removed the generic type parameter and its as-T assertion, so no type assertion remains on this path; callers narrow on the subcommand discriminant. typecheck, build, tests and release:check all pass against 2026.8.3. Superseded dependabot PR #51 (2026.7.31) was closed with an explanation. Bots: CodeRabbit, Greptile, DeepScan, Hound and semgrep all green with no actionable findings; Sourcery was rate-limited."
body: ""
